id:                     E331
trigger_tool:           git|buildbot|checkout-pr
phase:                  pre-pr|checkout
error_signature:        archives/a/<lowercase-package>/... already exists in working directory|CI_PACKAGES received: archives/.../<Uppercase>/... archives/.../<lowercase>/...

severity:               2
category:               git|windows|case-insensitive|rename|buildbot
match_keywords:         case-only rename, case-insensitive worktree, already exists in working directory, git apply --3way, checkout-pr, CI_PACKAGES, deletion-only old path, Conan slug
title:                  Make case-only archive renames three-way replayable

root_cause:             A patch that only changes path casing represents two Git paths that alias the same physical file on a case-insensitive checkout. Direct git apply rejects the lowercase destination as already present. If any file remains as a deletion-only old-case path, changed-package discovery can emit the uppercase package token; empty blobs are especially problematic because aggregate diff rename detection does not pair them reliably.
affected_scope:         Pull requests that lowercase Conan archive paths or otherwise perform case-only Git renames while CI reconstructs the PR through a patch on a case-insensitive worker.
verification_cmd:       Export the exact staged candidate diff against current main; require its changed-path list and projected package directories to contain only the lowercase package; require no uppercase recipe or package-input path in the candidate; prove direct apply fails without partial changes, then require git apply --3way to return zero and reproduce the exact candidate tree, path set, and per-file identities.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           content-bearing-case-rename-with-three-way-replay
rec_description:        When a merged-but-unpublished recipe requires a new numeric repair version, change both the package-directory case and version segment and migrate every tracked file, including empty sentinels, so the destination cannot alias the old path. If the exact version must remain, use content-bearing renames plus three-way replay and handle empty files through an unambiguous temporary path or a separate CI selector fix; never retain an old-case remnant. Require lower-only changed-package projection and exact current-main replay.
rec_command:            git diff --binary <base> <candidate-tree> > candidate.diff; git apply --3way --index candidate.diff; git write-tree
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               git-case-only-rename-replay

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      two-commit-rename
fallback_description:   When the hosting or CI patch path cannot perform a three-way replay, use an intermediate unambiguous path in one commit and the lowercase destination in a second commit, then verify the provider's actual PR diff.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       git mv.*[A-Z].*git mv.*[a-z].*without.*replay
forbid_1_reason:        Local index success on Windows does not prove that the server-generated PR patch is applicable on the CI worker.
forbid_1_consequence:   checkout-pr can fail before any recipe gate or build executes.

forbid_2_pattern:       delete.*old-case.*file.*without.*changed-path.*audit
forbid_2_reason:        A deletion-only old-case file can make the CI package selector emit both case variants; an empty blob may not be recoverable as a rename in the aggregate diff.
forbid_2_consequence:   The obsolete uppercase package token aliases the new recipe on a case-insensitive worker and fails the Conan slug gate.

forbid_3_pattern:       retry.*rebuild.*already exists in working directory
forbid_3_reason:        Rebuilding the same immutable revision cannot repair a deterministic patch application failure.
forbid_3_consequence:   Repeated CI runs consume capacity and preserve the same checkout failure.

principles:
